Original commit body from 77651e8ee3bc1ab81a6ac048634cdf67cc4b9509:

``interface IChild : IBase`` (C#) and ``type GChild interface { GBase;
N() }`` (Go) produced no edge: neither analyzer put the bases in
``meta["base_classes"]``, so the inheritance linker, which already turns
an interface source's bases into ``extends`` edges (WI-kalug), had
nothing to read.

- csharp.py: the interface branch calls ``_extract_base_list`` as the
  class and struct branches do.
- go.py: ``_extract_interface_embeddings`` lists an interface's
  single-term ``type_elem`` children (``GBase``, ``io.Reader`` as
  ``Reader``), unqualified like struct embedding; a type-set constraint
  (``~int | string``) is not an embedding.

End to end (``hypergumbo survey`` on the items' fixtures): ``extends
IChild -> IBase`` plus ``implements Impl -> IChild`` and the
``dispatches_to IBase.M -> Impl.M`` that now hangs off it; ``extends
GChild -> GBase``. Red: both interfaces had ``meta`` None.

The type-hierarchy linker's docstring said these two hops emit no edge
at all; corrected. The signature-axis registry cites two C# sites by
line; they moved with the insertion and the citations follow.

